# Fish cakes
(sardines, tinned) 2 tins (~4oz as stated)
(mayonnaise) 1/2 cup
(bread crumbs, Panko) 1/2 cup
(Old Bay seasoning) 2tsp
(egg) 1
(lemon juice, optional) as desired
# Sauce
(yogurt, plain, whole milk) 1/2 cup
(sriracha) 1tbsp
(mustard, Dijon) 1tbsp
(Worcestershire sauce) 1tsp
(garlic, minced, optional) as desired

::equipment

(bowl)
(fork)
(baking sheet, rimmed) -OR- (pan, large, cast iron) -OR- (casserole dish)
(refrigerator)
(oven)

::instructions

(sardines) <remove, tins, reserve oil>
{cake mix} = (sardines) + (mayonnaise) + (bread crumbs) + (Old Bay seasoning) + (egg) + (sardines, oil) from one tin / ~2TB
Optional [
    {cake mix} + (lemon juice)
]
{cake mix} <mix, gently, fork, incorporated not puréed>
    <scoop, small balls>
    <flatten, patties 2in across and ~1/2in thick>
    <place, rimmed baking sheet or large cast iron pan or casserole dish>
    <refrigerate, ~30m>
Meanwhile [
    {yogurt sauce} = (yogurt) + (sriracha) + (mustard) + (Worcestershire sauce)
    Optional [
        {yogurt sauce} + (garlic)
    ]
    {yogurt sauce} <mix>
]
(oven) <adjust, rack top third>
{fish cakes} <broil, 5m>
    <turn>
    <broil, 3-5m more, until golden brown>
    <drizzle, lemon juice, source final step>
    <serve, hot, yogurt sauce>

::notes
Can be served with a Spicy Yogurt Sauce as Tapas or Hors D’Oeuvres.
